Package: pve-update-manager
Version: @VERSION@
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Maintainer: pve-update-manager <pve-update-manager@localhost>
License: AGPL-3+
Depends: pve-manager (>= 9.0), pve-container, libpve-common-perl, libpve-storage-perl, perl
Description: Update Manager tab for Proxmox VE containers and nodes
 Adds an "Update Manager" tab to every LXC container, to every node and to the
 datacenter in the Proxmox VE web interface.
 .
 The container tab is a text box: the update commands for that container are
 written by hand, stored under /etc/pve/pve-update-manager/, and run inside the
 container by pressing Update. Nothing is generated.
 .
 The node and datacenter tabs list the hosts and every container. Tick the ones
 that should be updated and they run one after another, each leaving its own
 recorded state and its own task log - which the row then shows. A setting
 starts them all at once instead. The datacenter tab spans the whole cluster,
 and there the servers always work in parallel with each other.
 .
 Before a container is updated it is snapshotted, where its storage can take
 one, so a bad upgrade can be rolled back; the oldest above a retention count
 are removed after the run. Every save of a target's commands is kept as well,
 and can be put back from the editor.
 .
 A node can also run its updates on a timer: the Settings window sets when (a
 systemd calendar event such as 03:00 or mon..fri 02:30), which targets are
 included, and whether they run at the same time or one after another (one
 after another by default).
 .
 The integration is four one-line edits to files owned by pve-manager (a script
 tag in index.html.tpl and a require in pvedaemon, pveproxy and pvesh). They are
 re-applied automatically after a pve-manager upgrade by a dpkg trigger, and
 removed again when this package is.
